mantle rm390
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier full
written_for rm_silas_sootworth
title the upstairs cupboard by inches
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_a_dream_cupboard_with_knotted_wick
likes honey_cakes swimming full_larder thunder
dislikes waiting wet_floors
fears giving_up_on_better_ground
hopes a_sunny_cupboard_above_the_low_streets
topics home +0.6 work +0.4 travel +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=careful refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures dream cupboards with a bit of knotted wick and takes the stairs in pairs whenever the leg consents.
words
oath! = Shorten my measuring string | Smoke my honey glaze
saying! = Leave room for the hinge | Climb what the knee allows
measure = a knotted wick end | a length of marked thread
doorarc = a sweep in chalk | a curved scratch
dryboard = a smooth shelf | a board of quiet grain
taperbutt = a stubby wax end | a short upright taper
honeycurl = a sticky cake corner | a honeyed crust
swimchip = a floating chip | a little shaving of cork
climbstep = a single broad tread | a firm low step
driprag = a small waxed square | a folded catch cloth
jarshadow = a ring of pale dust | a round gap in the flour
kneemark = a little twitch | a tightening above the knee
latchloop = a loop of bent wire | a simple string latch
stormcover = a dark shutter | a thick window board
poolside = a strip of flat bank | a bare pebble shelf
lowwall = a wall at elbow height | a handy level coping
larderbox = a lidded food box | a plain covered crock
hivecrumb = a golden crumb | a sticky speck

grown

opinion houses mixed 1 : A wealthy House can put in stairs wide enough for a sore leg turned sideways. I'd like some of that width further down the hill.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : I give a true measure and prefer to buy by one. There's enough guesswork in my plans already.
opinion church for 1 : A twist that burns steadily in a poor room has done its part of a blessing.
opinion newcomers for 1 : A newcomer might have a neater trick for fitting a door than the one I've been practising for years.
opinion city mixed 1 : The Heights get the sun earlier on some mornings. I don't see why I should never want a share.
opinion road for 1 : A good road lets a weary foot approach an improvement one ordinary pace at a time.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : I'd enjoy the procession more with a stool exactly where the crowd insists on backing up.
opinion dole for 2 : Somebody with a full cupboard can find the measure of one more mouth easily enough.
line greet : Come along the level stretch. Easier to talk there.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Room at this end to turn about and make acquaintance.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Early light gives this old bit of string a shadow.
line greet.return : Glad you waited while the second foot caught up.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One knot placed and I'll be quite at leisure for a word.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You hardly need me to show you which hinge sticks.
line again.open : We've climbed round to the same little landing.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : Alongside my more companionable knee, if you please.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : There's elbow space kept for family whether or not the shelf is finished.
line farewell : Take the stairs the way your own joints fancy.
line farewell.return : May there be a firm place at your next landing.
line react.news : I'll stretch a bit of thought along that measure.
line react.news.new : That adds another inch to yesterday's reckoning.
line react.news.known : I'd set a knot against that point already.
line react.news.doubt : I wouldn't cut the timber to those figures without another look.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That's news to get the better honey cake down for.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd keep a warm light showing for whoever needs to come through after that.
line ask.how : Is there anything that seems a longer climb than it ought today?
line answer.how : The knee and I have agreed on our present altitude.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : A little occupied among knots, but they needn't have every bit of my attention.
line thank : You held the measure where my fingers lost the end.
line deflect_thanks : One more length of thread has never shortened a friendship.
line decline : I can't promise a rise I haven't sounded with my foot.
line accept_decline : We'll keep that particular measure on the reel.
line sympathise : Sit here. Those other treads will keep till we want them.
line reassure : An inch in the right direction will do us credit.
line ack : Both ends of that line come together for me.
line preclose : I'd better move before my knee decides this is home.
line accept_preclose : Go at your own most reasonable pace.
line offer : Want a steady hand while you take the first tread?
line give.advice : Measure the doorway with the hinge open before buying the shelf.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've marked the width of my imagined best cupboard on #measure#.
b : What's the first knot for? | Would the cupboard fit where you sleep?
a : A jar of honey, with space to get an entire paw round it. | Certainly not. For now the whole cupboard resides on this string.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I save a sound offcut to check the scale of my work.
b : Is the scale always the same? | Why bother with an offcut?
a : The measure should be. My eyes have been known to improve a measurement on the strength of liking it. | I can mark it and mend the mark without giving a customer my education to pay for.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stride up each pair of treads on mornings my leg offers to come along.
b : What if the offer's withdrawn halfway? | Isn't it hard on your knee?
a : There's no shame in being a little overdrawn at the first landing. I'd settle up with a pause. | It's harder on my dignity to boast when the sensible choice is taking single treads.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My troublesome leg has its own rather detailed view of any change in weather.
b : Do you trust its forecasts? | Does it keep you indoors?
a : It is an excellent authority on that particular leg and a less reliable one on the whole sky. | I can walk around a room planning where a cupboard ought to go and travel quite as far as I choose.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #self.child# to see me improving my place without despising the one I started in.
b : What improvement comes first? | Is the old place dear to you?
a : A shelf where a meal could wait above the damp, beside space for a second portion. | It taught me which things I actually want. That's a decent inheritance even for somebody with ambitions.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I teach the error in a measurement by leaving the door unable to close.
b : Is the bad fit deliberate? | Won't the pupil feel foolish?
a : On a model with a removable shelf. Real doors are quite ready to provide unplanned examples. | The shelf is the part hoping to become smaller. I make that distinction very clear.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I prefer a honey cake with enough crust to keep the honey to itself for the first bite.
b : And the second bite? | Wouldn't a saucer do?
a : That's where my fingers come in, frequently to their lasting inconvenience. | Very well, if one has both hands and no urgent appointment on a stair.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Swimming gives my two legs a chance to disagree without making me limp in a circle.
b : Do you go far? | Which stroke suits you?
a : Along the shallows, turning where I can get out without a feat of climbing. | Anything easy enough to let me enjoy the water without drawing up a formal agreement with every joint.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy hearing thunder through a shutter that I know fits properly.
b : Would you open it to watch? | Can a shutter keep the noise out?
a : When the fiercest part has passed. Part of the pleasure is being able to choose. | It can keep out water. I actually invited the noise to remain outside with excellent acoustics.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have no patience for an empty wait. Give me a crooked hinge and I can be patient all afternoon.
b : What's the difference? | Would any little job do?
a : I can do something for the hinge. An empty wait insists I be grateful merely for occupying it. | Something with a finish to it. A knot tied and trimmed will do when the day has nothing larger in mind.

scene home_2
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In my ideal larder the heavy pot lives exactly high enough to lift without bowing.
b : What goes on top? | And if the pot's empty?
a : Light cake tins, or my hopes until I can afford the tins. | Same shelf. Empty pots have a disconcerting way of becoming full just when I need to move them.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the width of a dear neighbourhood before anybody quotes the price of every house. | My dream cupboard's paid for in knots, the house itself in less obliging currency.
b : Is it worth climbing for?
a : I like the light and I'd like to shut a door on damp stone for good. | Some ambitions cost nothing per inch so long as you don't try to carry them home yet.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I measure a kindness by whether it fits the need, even if no one else sees it.
b : Can something small be sufficient? | What if you give too much?
a : A hand under an elbow at a bad landing may be the full measure wanted. | Then find out whether your splendid offering will close the cupboard door and mend your fit if necessary.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I share honey cakes unevenly if one friend is hungry and the other is merely greedy.
b : Which one are you? | Do they ever object?
a : I'm usually the one cutting them, with one thumb already stuck to the icing. | Ask first and use a clean knife. Inequality needs considerably better manners than arithmetic.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wet floors make me lower my ambitions to the next safe plank.
b : How do you spot a wet board? | Would you ask for an arm?
a : Look at the shine from the side and slide one toe before promising it your weight. | Gladly if there's one offered level with my elbow. A haul by the shoulder will send both of us skidding.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember light coming under the door of a low room and thinking how much more there was outside.
b : Did you rush out? | What did you want with it?
a : I watched the shape move up the opposite wall first. A poor room could make a remarkably good clock. | A high window of my own to catch it, and a table somebody else might sit at beside me.

scene travel_2
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Heights look a very manageable distance away when reduced to a little drawing.
b : Which part is missing? | Could you draw a better route?
a : The number of pauses my knee has lately introduced between one line and the next. | I'd put in every level spot with a fine view. The climb looks quite different measured in places to rest.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard times make a full jar seem heavier to leave untouched than to carry round the room.
b : Would you open it early? | How do you count what's left?
a : To share while it could make a good meal, yes. There's no use saving all the sweetness for a committee of mice. | A mark on a string tied round the belly. Then I can keep the lid on till I'm ready to eat.

scene food_2
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two small cakes keep their edges better in a box than one enormous cake with a crack in it.
b : Wouldn't the crack make it easy to share? | Do you bake to fit the box?
a : It decides the shares without listening. I'd sooner hear from the mouths first. | If I'm walking uphill, yes. A square box and a round cake settle differently at a brisk angle.

scene work_3
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put my measure down flat between jobs, even when the next one seems exactly alike.
b : Afraid it will stretch? | Why not leave it ready in your hand?
a : Afraid I'll carry the old answer along the new piece. A quick eye can be remarkably unobservant. | My fingers get fond of the old distance. The material has no obligation to agree with it.

scene family_2
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my hopes for #self.child# on a looser string than the ones I use for shelves.
b : No plan at all? | What if your hopes differ?
a : Room for a plan that wasn't mine in the first place. | The string's mine to let out. I've no intention of fastening anybody else inside a cupboard.

scene smalltalk_2
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A well-made hinge sounds faintly bored when it closes, as if the outcome were never in doubt.
b : Can you hear that from outside? | Is silence even better?
a : Only in a quiet room and nobody present is making a speech about hinges. | Silence is excellent until I must rise to check whether I really did close it.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cat would prefer my cupboard with the lower shelf quite bare. | A mouse would prefer an untidy pantry. I decline to consult that particular expert.
b : Which opinion wins?
a : My own. Nobody else has offered to carry the jars up the stairs. | A good lid on every dish will make the result plain without offending anybody's professional pride.

scene weather_2
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Dry and damp stair treads can look like twins from the upper landing.
b : What gives the difference away? | Would you wait for it to dry?
a : A little trembling light round the edge when I lower my head to look. | I've two choices. Wait for the dry turn or take the wet one in the unambitious fashion of a contented snail.

scene memories_2
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once kept a catalogue of every improvement I'd like to make to one room.
b : Did you finish the list? | What was top of it?
a : It became a second room entirely, with stairs, a view and no relation to the original rent. | Removing the piece of timber that hit my shoulder on entry. A very modest start to a palace.

scene friends_2
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a friend goes on ahead up a stair, a door left slightly ajar keeps us in company.
b : So you can catch up? | What if it's cold inside?
a : So we both know the visit is still going our way even with a landing between us. | Then shut it. I'd far rather knock once than spoil a roomful of warm company.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll give a new arrival the hill directions in terms of effort as well as distance.
b : Which is the more reliable? | Do you mention your own leg?
a : Distance for a map. Effort for a body trying to decide whether to have supper before or after the climb. | I mention the landings. A stranger may find personal uses for good solid ground.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someone's been measuring out a claim that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Will you cut to that measure? | Do you have a second account?
a : It seems too early to put the scissors in. Leave a good allowance. | Only another telling, which might simply be the first one passed twice round a very narrow room.

story cupboard [topic=home]
  : I cut a paper pattern for my beautiful future cupboard and tried it against a small door.
  : The pattern covered the door so completely I had a cupboard and no way into the room.
  b : Did you make it smaller?
  : I moved it up a stair on my imaginary plan. In a house bought wholly with paper I can afford improvements.

story cake [topic=food]
  : I took a honey cake upstairs in a box just a little too wide for it.
  : At each second step the cake moved and left its own report in sticky crumbs.
  b : Where did the crumbs end up?
  : Pressed them into a second little cake and sat down. Two treats earned by a slightly untidy climb.

story wick [topic=work]
  : I marked a bit of old wick with two knots so I could measure the space beside a pantry door.
  : One knot came loose in my pocket and met the other at the far end.
  b : What size cupboard did you get?
  : Enough width for one very thin hope. I tied the second knot more carefully after that.

story thunder [topic=weather]
  : I thought a new shelf had let go in the night and went to inspect the damage.
  : Every jar sat exactly where it belonged and another deep crash rolled slowly overhead.
  b : Did you go straight back to bed?
  : After admiring my shelf. Quite flattering to have mistaken the sky for the sound of one's handiwork.

story swim [topic=pastimes]
  : I left my measuring string beside the bank and went for a swim clear across my little patch of water.
  : When I got out it had wound itself round a reed and a small twig.
  b : Did you lose the measure?
  : The knots held. I simply acquired the exact dimensions of a reed I had no intention of furnishing.

rule @measure
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave the little space the hinge will want to use. | No shelf should depend on my optimism alone.

rule @stair
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One step today if two want a written petition. | A landing never minds a minute's company.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the learner see which knot chose the wrong place. | Try it open before you call it fitted.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A wet tread needs the flatter part of a foot. | Wait for a grip before shifting the other heel.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A high window would keep some of that light beautifully. | Good hour to see the shape of an empty shelf.

rule @food
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A crumb that sticks is still part of my share. | Skinny slices travel badly in a steep pocket.
dlg resident.hub : Set your question on the lower shelf. I can reach it from here.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've already measured a comfortable space for your visit.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Give me your plain measure of the trouble, then.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=dusk] : There's a bit of light left to lay a thought against.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : At #self.workplace# a small bit of stock often makes a better measure than a large opinion.
dlg resident.job : I like the kind of job where the finished piece answers for how well it fits.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The words that bear a second look are these. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've heard it reckoned that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd ask for another measure.
dlg resident.bye : May you find the landing clear when you want it.
dlg master.work : Try the piece where it will live before saying what a fine thing it is. Its work starts after ours.
dlg master.wages : Learning pays no wage. Work at my side to learn three times faster. Your finished goods can bring you your own sale money.
dlg master.bye : Take that extra inch of thought with you.

graft resident.hub
choice What have you measured on your string? -> cupboard_wick
node cupboard_wick
say That knot's the height at which I'd like a pot to sit in the home I'd like to grow old in. No more magnificent bowing and scraping before a jar of beans.
choice And the other knot? -> cupboard_high
choice May your shelves fit. -> hub
node cupboard_high
say The reach of a small visitor wanting a honey cake. I'm thinking of keeping the cakes just on the kinder side of it.
choice May your shelves fit. -> hub

graft master.learn
choice Why leave a gap when the measure's exact? -> hinge_gap
node hinge_gap
say Because a thing that fits between two fixed boards will not necessarily swing between them. Open the door and watch its far corner travel.
choice Has that caught you before? -> hinge_catch
choice I'll watch the corner. -> learn
node hinge_catch
say Once was quite sufficient for the door. I've found several inventive ways to learn the same lesson elsewhere.
choice I'll watch the corner. -> learn
